Selected source is incorporated into the CMA application. It is not exported
as a reusable component library. Original paths and SHA-256 hashes are recorded
in source-map.json. No separately identified third-party notices appear in
these selected source files.

Mechanical extraction: topographic-field.ts is split into seeded elevation
noise and contour helpers. The flat Flow shaders are extracted from
topographic-surface.ts with export declarations. Application lifetime, theme,
and rendering-budget adaptations are recorded separately in source-map.json.

CMA adaptation selects only ordinary solid Flow: fixed seed 42, scale 270,
density 5, distortion 2.4, line width 1.1, opacity .85, speed .32. Grain,
hover, gradients, dashed lines, Terrain and animated Canvas2D fallback are
omitted. The surface is synchronous; CMA owns bounded playback and theme
policy. Resource acquisition/disposal is transactional and faults use fixed
categories. No runtime asset, shader or package is fetched from upstream.

The static SVG masks in ../../assets are derived from the same seeded field
and contour algorithms. Their alpha masks use CMA theme tokens for color.
The full RCL text is also retained in the browser surface module's license
comment. See source-map.json for exact source spans and adaptation details.
